      "document_id": "DOC001",
      "content": "The AND operator returns true only if both conditions are true. The OR operator is represented by two vertical bars (||). With the OR operator, if at least one condition is true, the result is true. In a loan eligibility example, an applicant is eligible if they have high income OR good credit. When evaluating an OR expression, Java evaluates from the left; if the left side is true, the right side is not evaluated.",
